// Position matrix (design 235), grid 3 "Graph shapes" — row: 3-cycle.
// `a` -> `b` -> `c` -> `a` is named the same way the 2-cycle is
// (graph_2cycle_error.saw), whole loop in the message and every edge's line in
// the hint. Kept as its own row so the grid does not assume a longer cycle
// behaves like the short one without evidence.
//
// The walk is depth-first over SORTED keys and sorted successors, so a given
// program always names the same cycle — a diagnostic that varied with dict
// order would be worse than none.
//
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: import cycle: modules.graphcyc3.a -> modules.graphcyc3.b -> modules.graphcyc3.c -> modules.graphcyc3.a
// EXPECT-ERROR-ABSENT: undefined function

import modules.graphcyc3.a

func main() {
    print("{a.alpha()}")
}
